1. User scans QR using EcoDrop App
            ↓
2. ESP32 receives authentication from the app
            ↓
3. ESP32 unlocks the intake door
            ↓
4. User places the waste item
            ↓
5. Door closes automatically
            ↓
6. IR sensor confirms an object is present
            ↓
7. Load cell measures the weight
            ↓
8. Raspberry Pi camera captures the image
            ↓
9. Raspberry Pi runs the AI model
            ↓
10. AI identifies:
      • Waste category
      • Item type
      • Confidence score
            ↓
11. Raspberry Pi estimates the reward
      (based on waste type, weight, and valuation rules)
            ↓
12. Raspberry Pi sends the result to the ESP32
            ↓
13. ESP32 displays:
      • Item name
      • Weight
      • Estimated EcoCoins
      • Accept / Reject prompt
            ↓
14. User accepts through the mobile app
            ↓
15. ESP32 rotates the sorting mechanism
            ↓
16. Waste drops into the correct bin
            ↓
17. ESP32 updates Firebase
            ↓
18. EcoCoins are credited to the user's account




